  "reason": "RNA multiprofile scvi is currently the strongest direction, while image-only ResNet50 is weak even with multiprofile avgpool. The key uncertainty is whether the image modality can become useful with a stronger image representation before spending budget on multimodal fusion. config_014 changes only the image encoder from ResNet50 to ImageNet ViT-L while keeping multiprofile and avgpool, making it directly comparable to config_011. It tests whether image representation quality is the bottleneck; if ViT substantially improves image-only performance, multimodal ViT configurations become more promising, otherwise the search can focus on RNA-only improvements. This isolates one important design choice and avoids confounding image encoder and fusion effects."
